# Every pull request requests a review from both owners, and GitHub drops the
# author, so each of us is asked to review the other's work without anyone
# remembering to add them. `main` requires one approving review from a
# non-author, and this is what puts the right name on it.
#
# Both entries need write access for the request to be made at all. Order does
# not matter: every listed owner is requested, not just the last match.
#
# GET-claude cannot do this. CODEOWNERS is a paid feature on private
# repositories, and that one is private on a free plan, so its pull requests
# name a reviewer at creation time instead.

